WEBVTT

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.950
The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.920
Once upon a time,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.250
an old man went up a mountain to cut bamboo.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.210
Oh?

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.660
Shining bamboo!

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.980
Scary! What is this, a mutation?

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.120
A ghost? The occult? Cattle mutilation?

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.390
That's totally off...

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.350
What on earth is this...

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.830
Autumn.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.750
Winter.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.070
Spring, Summer, Autumn.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.480
...happened about a year ago.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.030
Why are you only telling me now?

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.050
That was my new year's first dream!

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.360
No one cares.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.680
C'mon Sonya-chan, you don't have to be so cold just because it's winter—

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.950
I want to eat mochi…

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.120
Mochi?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.080
Don’t you know what mochi is?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.720
It’s like this white mushy kind of food.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.690
Wait, do they call it mochi because it’s mushy?

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.550
What a revelation!

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:07.920
I’d better write this down…

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.090
I don't get it, but good for you.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.490
That reminds me of something I'd heard about it.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.910
Apparently it has no poison, but you can still kill people by making them eat it.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.140
No no, it's not like it always gets stuck in your throat!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.980
And making it is fun, too!

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.410
It's called Mochitsuki.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.310
I think I've seen that before.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.820
That wooden hammer looks pretty strong.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.480
You really do see everything as a weapon...

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.780
I want to have you try Mochitsuki...

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.260
Though I'm sure this school wouldn't have a mortar or hammer...

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.060
It does!

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:47.310
Agiri-san's voice??

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.080
Where from?

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.470
She just called.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.430
I heard you talking about Mochitsuki.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:58.130
I'll prepare everything in the clubroom, so drop by later.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.410
Yay!

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:02.910
But why do you have a Mochitsuki set?

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.980
It's a basic tool for ninjas.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.270
Do you use it for techniques or training or something?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:15.030
No, but freshly pounded mochi is delicious!

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.230
After school.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.510
And on that note,

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.930
we've come to have Sonya-chan try out Mochitsuki!

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.430
I'm fine not doing this, you know.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.790
She's not here.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.900
There's the mortar and hammer!

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.750
Let's practice before Agiri-san gets here!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.570
Wh-Why...

00:04:56.570 --> 00:05:01.100
I figured she was hiding somewhere, but I didn't think...

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.020
Welcome!

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.920
That gave me a fright...

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.140
Body substitution technique again?

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.940
I didn't use that at all.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.720
Perhaps you're mistaking it for body clone technique?

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.210
Here's the real mortar!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.430
I've also steamed the sticky rice.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.150
Oh, okay...

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.670
Well, let's start over!

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.600
You can start the pounding first.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.160
Don't stumble and fall over now! Aim for the mochi!

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.870
Alright, let's go!

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:41.650
It's over there! Over there!

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.280
Amateurs are so useless!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.770
I'll show you how it's done!

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.950
Though, this thing is actually pretty heavy...

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:58.730
I prepared a lighter one just in case!

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.530
Yay! This will be a lot easier to use!

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:07.320
I'm no expert, but I'm pretty sure you can't pound with that.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.020
You're such an amateur.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.650
It's all about how you use the tool!

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:16.280
Allow me to show you how it's done!

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:18.110
Listen to the boss!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.550
Pound mochi!

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.700
Do it, do it, do it!

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:26.340
Not me, the mochi!

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.020
The mochi!

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.160
I love you.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:30.960
Oh, you...

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.820
You don't have to get so mad at a joke!

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.980
Anyway, it doesn't matter what tools we use, as long as we have mochi in the end.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.360
There's no way you're making any with that thing.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.250
Then we'll have a contest to see who can make mochi without the hammer.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.810
Whoever loses doesn't get any!

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.350
I have no idea where that came from, but you're on!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.160
Let's see... What can I use?

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.160
How about this?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.620
This is good! With one pierce...

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.740
What happened to the Mochitsuki battle?

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.000
Alright, the mochi's ready!

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.200
She did it already?!

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:13.130
Well, the sticky rice was getting cold...

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.810
So this is mochi?

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:20.440
Alright, show me how to use it.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.180
You mean when people choke on it?

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.770
Here!

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.390
Thanks!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:30.280
That won't happen if you're careful when you eat it.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:32.970
So good!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.820
Well that's boring.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.660
I guess I'll have some too.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.520
Here you go.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:46.940
What? You already had yours, greedy pig.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.020
So annoying. What is it?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.720
Your neck?

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.750
What about it?

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.460
You want to be strangled?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.260
No! Mochi got stuck in my throat!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.020
Weren't you saying how that doesn't happen?

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.110
And why would you think I wanted you to choke me?

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.430
That's just weird! Right, Agiri-san?

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.550
I thought she was being too quiet...

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.620
I'm sure she's using a feign death technique, right?

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.920
Alright, come on.

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:38.450
Substitution's substitution technique.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:42.310
Killtaro.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:54.160
Once upon a time in Japan, there was an assassin called Killtaro who completed every job without fail.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.700
Peaches.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:56.650
Delicious!

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:04.820
One day, Killtaro took on a request to exterminate demons.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.560
Hey, it's Killtaro-san!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.930
I'm a huge fan of yours!

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.450
Where are you going?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.590
Get lost, stray dog!

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.790
Let me come with you!

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.340
You're annoying, so no.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.720
I'll follow you anyway!

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.380
Don't underestimate a dog's tracking skills!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:29.970
Woof woof woof woof woof woof
woof woof woof woof woof

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.530
I'll give you a reward as a loyal follower then.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.450
Millet dumplings!

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.610
I've always wanted to try one!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.510
Killtaro-san!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.710
A pheasant?

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:59.330
I heard you're going to exterminate some demons.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:01.620
Just so you know, I'm not taking you.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.100
That's not it...

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:06.860
Demon slayer!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.640
I'll make it cheap for you!

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.820
What do you think?

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.540
No, I'm fine.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.480
Killtaro-san! I'm a monkey!

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.380
I'll do anything, so take me with you! Please!

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.080
Mortar!

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:35.700
Bee!

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.250
Chestnuts!

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.730
Crab!

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:47.550
Why is this happening to me?!

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:48.780
What's this?

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:49.330
You can have it.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:58.090
After a journey filled with trials and battles, Killtaro finally reached the island of demons.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.400
So this is the island of demons?

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:15.650
Peaches...

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:22.870
Delicious!

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:26.580
Someone's eating our peaches!

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.830
They're being stolen!

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.420
Scandalous!

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:36.210
How could you eat the peaches that these children worked so hard to grow?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.610
So cruel! What a demon! A demon!

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:50.110
You demon! Demon! Demon! Demon! Demon!

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:02.310
Thereafter, the island became known as Demon Island.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:05.590
And everybody lived happily ever—

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.310
That wasn't happy at all!

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.250
Zombie Baby!

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.850
This way's no good either.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:27.040
Sonya-chan, leave this to me!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:28.600
I have some items!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.750
Really?

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:36.980
Begone, evil spirits!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.670
That's for vampires!!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:44.550
Dammit!

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.430
She just made it worse!

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.900
I'm going to suck your blood!

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.310
And she's still got it wrong!

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:55.060
Morning!

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:58.290
Oh no! We're going to burn away!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.750
Like I said, that's vampires.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.800
Farewell, everyone!

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:10.680
The power of self suggestion...

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:15.430
That was my new year's first dream!

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.330
How about you just leave it at one.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:21.830
Sonya-chan!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:24.530
Do you want to play Fukuwarai or Sugoroku?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.020
What's that?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.710
Traditional Japanese games played on New Year!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.380
Let's play together!

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.680
Not interested.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:34.580
We totally have to! It'll be fun!

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.260
Here's the blindfold and dice!

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.360
No thanks.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.690
Fine, then there's a curse if you don't!

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:41.130
What do you mean "then"?!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:45.350
Too bad, if you decide you want to play later, it'll be too late.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.880
I got 5!

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:52.200
Eyebrows...

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.420
Whoops, a turn-around. Go back 2.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:05.470
Oh, 9! Nice, I get the stomach!

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:08.130
This makes no sense!

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.310
Ta da!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:16.230
I actually prepared another traditional Japanese game!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.240
What do you think this is?

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.100
A kite?

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:21.210
Nope, it's a squid!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.300
How can you not see that, you squidhead—

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:28.290
And if I had answered squid, you would have said it was a kite.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.280
Right you are.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:32.170
After school.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:35.460
Did we have to make a detour all the way out here?

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:38.440
Yep. There's a good wind today.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.830
I see.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.340
Well, have fun.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:44.330
Why leave? It'll be fun!

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.790
Fine then.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:50.110
I'll use this kite with your portrait on it so I don't get lonely.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:52.780
Hey!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.070
Let's go!

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.600
Don't just watch! Help me!

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.760
You seemed to be having fun already.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.450
Hold this and run with it.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.070
It's cold. I don't want to run.

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:12.410
Good pace! Keep that up!

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:14.920
Kite strings hurt...

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:17.280
I'm sure you can fly a kite by yourself.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.590
How?

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:21.600
Use a shorter length of string first, then run with that.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.800
I kind of look like a ham now...

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:24.920
Listen!

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.500
Okay then, show me!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.340
What a hassle...

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.170
If you run like this,

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:32.890
it'll slowly rise—

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.130
Like that.

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:38.960
Get it?

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:41.540
You fell!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.110
I'm sorry, I understand.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.100
Like this... Whoops, I fell.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.070
I'm going to break this.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.440
Please, no! I'll be serious!

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:02.430
Wow, it's flying!

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.650
Seeing a squid in the air is really weird.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:07.020
Really? I think it's cute.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.450
A crow!

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:14.520
It was shot down.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.260
It must have thought it was food.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.050
Do birds like squid?

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:20.110
I have no idea.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:21.390
Fine then.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:24.310
I'll just do this...

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.530
Alright! No crows!

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.930
Now it's even weirder.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.940
Other people are flying kites too.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:35.840
They are!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.410
So high, too!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.590
Alright, I'll go compete with them!

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.540
Compete at what?

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.530
Damn you, Koheita!

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.790
Darling!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.010
Our strings tangled and they got mad at me...

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.000
Don't go over there.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:00.940
It's cold...

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:05.140
Hold this while I go buy something warm to drink.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:06.900
Why do I have to...

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:12.440
Oh no!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:21.770
You're so mean! You broke it!

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:22.980
Sorry.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.960
We can't get it up there...

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.140
Fine, we'll use the backup.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.260
Wait, that's...

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:31.310
It's fine!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.550
It looks like someone else now.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.630
Some<i>thing</i> else...

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.720
Yay!

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:43.100
Watch where you're running.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.270
It's fine! I won't cry if I fall!

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:47.140
And it's all grass around here anyway!

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.950
It's cold! Save me!

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:51.910
Like I said...

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.780
Save me! Hurry!

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:57.030
No thanks. You can reach the bottom anyway.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.710
How did she know?

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.700
I figured you were trying to drag me down with you.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.210
Anyway, are you okay with that?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.220
Wait! Wait!

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:09.880
Dammit! Dammit!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:12.600
Is that the string for that kite?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.710
Gotcha!

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:23.840
I'm so cold... At this rate, I'll die.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.440
Whose fault do you think this is?

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.020
Oh! Nice!

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:29.320
Let's go take a bath, Sonya-chan.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:30.370
What?

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:32.150
There's actually a bath here?

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.330
It's called a public bath.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:37.090
C'mon, if we don't hurry up, we'll catch a cold.

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.230
Two please.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.160
Go right ahead.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.430
What's with that guy?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.350
He's just the attendant.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.180
C'mon Sonya-chan, hurry up.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.850
What's wrong?

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:58.140
Don't tell me when you fell into the water, it made you forget how to unbutton your shirt?

00:18:58.140 --> 00:18:59.740
Of course not.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:03.000
I'm fine with not going in.

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.080
What're you talking about?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.680
We already paid.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:07.950
Well, uh...

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.550
First off, an assassin shouldn't be nude in public.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:12.610
You just made that up!

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:15.250
D-Don't tell me...

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:20.030
...she has a bunch of stuff on her body that she can't tell anyone about?!

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:21.990
C'mon! Take it off!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:24.260
I wanna wash your back!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.330
No thanks!

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.640
I don't want to know what you're planning by trying to wash my back.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.040
I won't do anything bad!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.940
See? Isn't this nice?

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:44.730
Yeah.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.920
Hello! I'm Yasuna!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:58.100
I'm a magical girl who came from the land of magic to train!

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:03.450
I always mess up, but I'm trying my best to become a splendid magical girl!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.010
And today, I'm...

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.090
...getting beat up in the ring.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:14.550
Hey! You shoulda dodged that punch!

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.890
I-I can't do it anymore.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.800
Let me concede!

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.340
Throw in the towel already!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:22.340
You idiot! I ain't doing that!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:26.310
You need to earn all the money needed to repair the roof of my gym!

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.360
No way...

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:35.660
I don't know if you're a magical-something-or-other, but you've got guts.

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:41.600
Y-You're good...

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.620
You too.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.510
Y-You're good.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:50.830
You too.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.950
Wait, you're not doing anything!

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:54.580
Stop trying to trick me!

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.440
I'm going to end you!

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.650
Now's my chance!

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.640
Milky Staff!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:03.980
Nice!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:06.050
Use whatever you have to win, even magic!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.390
Th-This is...

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:12.440
Carrot Max Forward Miracle!

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.230
Alright!

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.600
You moron!

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:21.120
What're you doing?!

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.630
That was my New Year's first dream.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.200
Do you understand what "first" dream means?

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.460
I wish I could use magic.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.070
Ridiculous.

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:40.030
How?

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.860
It might be possible.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.300
This is...

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.320
No way...

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.760
It's just a toy.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:51.010
We won't know till we try!

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:53.520
Carrot Max Forward Miracle!

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.740
Ta-da!

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:10.410
Bath, Kite, Mochi, First Dream of the Year.
